{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וביום השמיני", :translit "u'vayom ha'shemini", :gloss "and on the eighth day"} {:he "פסוק זה יש בו תיבות ואותיות כמו שבפ' ויכלו", :translit "pasuk zeh yesh bo tivot v'otiot k'mo she'b'parashat va'yakhulu", :gloss "this verse has words and letters like those in the section 'And they were completed'"} {:he "שמילה דוחה שבת", :translit "milah docheh shabbat", :gloss "circumcision overrides Sabbath"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse Leviticus 12:3 matches Genesis 2:1–3 in word count and letter count"}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Eliezer holds that all labor necessary for circumcision overrides Shabbat (Shabbat 132a, Yevamot 71b), based on the fact that Abraham's circumcision is dated to the eighth day regardless of which day of the week it fell on (Genesis 17:12). The passage 'Va'yakhulu' (Genesis 2:1–3) narrates the original Shabbat of creation.", :sources ["Shabbat 132a" "Yevamot 71b" "Genesis 17:12" "Genesis 2:1–3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וביום השמיני ימול בשר", :translit "u'vayom ha'shemini yimol basar", :gloss "and on the eighth day the flesh shall be circumcised"} {:he "שכל היום יהיה כשר למול", :translit "she'kol ha'yom yihyeh kasher l'mul", :gloss "that the entire day is valid to circumcise"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וביום השמיני ימול בשר", :b "שכל היום יהיה כשר למול"}], :frame {:text "The halakhah permits circumcision on the eighth day throughout the entire daytime, all day (Pesachim 59a; Yoreh De'ah 262:1). Some Rishonim note that it may even be performed after minchah, distinguishing it from other time-bound commandments (Pesachim 4a).", :sources ["Pesachim 59a" "Yoreh De'ah 262:1" "Pesachim 4a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse Leviticus 12:3 matches Genesis 2:1–3 in word count and letter count", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "וביום השמיני ימול בשר", :a-value 1067, :b "שכל היום יהיה כשר למול", :b-value 1067, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :leviticu